#%PAM-1.0
#
# Screen locker: a CREDENTIAL CHECK and nothing else.
#
# No `session` stack on purpose. cce-lock never calls pam_open_session — the
# user's session already exists; the locker only re-verifies the person in
# front of it. The greeter learned this the hard way: opening a session there
# ran pam_gnome_keyring's auto_start, a fork() out of a multi-threaded Vulkan
# process, which could wedge before exec and freeze login on
# "Authenticating..." (2026-09-18). A locker that did the same would freeze
# with the session still locked.
#
# No `password` stack either: a locker must never be a route to changing a
# password.

auth       include      system-local-login
account    include      system-local-login
